  "meta": {
    "title": "Why Almost Nobody Lives in the Middle of Australia 🇦🇺🤯",
    "description": "Australia 🇦🇺 is a giant continent, but almost 80% of Australians live within 25 km of the coast 🏖️ Why? 80% of the land gets less than 600 mm of rain a year and half gets less than 300 mm 🏜️ The Great Dividing Range runs almost 4,000 km along the east coast, and the interior, the Outback, is desert and semi-desert. That's why Australia has only about 3.5 people per km², with 27 million people living mostly on the edges 🤯",
    "pinnedComment": [
      "80% of Australians live near the coast 🤯🇦🇺",
      "Aussies: coast or Outback, where do you live? 👇",
      "Which country's population map next? 🗺️"
    ],
